<title>UK: Algeria offers to freeze Nov gas oil prices - trade.</title>
<headline>Algeria offers to freeze Nov gas oil prices - trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Algerian oil company Sonatrach has asked contract holders for no change to its low sulphur gas oil prices in November, contract holders said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said Sonatrach had asked to keep unchanged its $2.50 per tonne premium to the formula, which is based on diesel prices in northern Europe and the Mediterranean.</p>
<p>Negotiations would be completed by week's end at the latest. Traders said Sonatrach was expected to deliver five or six cargoes in November.</p>
<p>-- William Maclean, London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
